'''Ancient Egg: N204''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be unlocked by playing the [[Lunar New Year (Event Gacha)|Lunar New Year]] [[Cat Capsule#Collaboration Event Capsule|Event Cat Capsule]]. It was added in [[Version 13.1 Update|Version 13.1]] for [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], and [[Version 14.0 Update|Version 14.0]] for all other versions.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 730
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Ancient Egg: N204
|name2 = Cinnabar Egg: N204
|name3 = Lion Dancer Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cinnabar Egg: N204''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Lion Dancer Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
While this unit seems amazing on the surface with its variety of abilities, it tragically suffers from [[Single Attack]], which, combined with its poor stats, limits its offensive potential and weaken capabilities. Even with Behemoth Slayer, it has poor matchups against theoretically viable targets. For [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]], the only one it can reach is [[Wild Doge]], while [[Cumulus Gallus]] and [[Elephantidae Papaou]] outrange it and deal too much damage for it to handle. Against [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] Behemoths, it can't reach [[Infernal Pegasus Deonil]] since it lacks [[Immune to Freeze|Freeze Immunity]] and [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]], and although it does decently against [[Casaurian Ahirujo]], [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] already existed to counter him.

Outside of Behemoth enemies, this unit fares a little better, but not much. Far superior alternatives exist for both traits, and it struggles to reach relevant threats in the first place, let alone engage them.

